# Golden digests for benches/vt_workloads.rs. Do not edit by hand.
#
# Reference: diri 589d0a46c (origin/main), regenerated after #924's
# declared history retention change (its LZ codec skips faster through
# text that does not repeat, so the 4 MiB budget keeps fewer rows: ascii
# 63537 -> 63313 generated / 63793 -> 63569 kitten, unicode 54608 ->
# 54128 both). Only history row counts, scrollback cells/metadata and the
# links digest changed; every other field of every workload is identical
# to the previous reference (0b54ea089, and 3fc4feb66 with #921's
# c23006a27 before it). Built in release and fed one byte per read with
# the OSC checksum on, generated and kitten capture sections both:
#
#   cargo build --release -p diri-terminal-state --features bench-verify --bench vt_workloads
#   DIRI_VT_BENCH_GOLDEN=$PWD/crates/diri-terminal-state/benches/vt_workloads.golden <bench binary> --bench
#   DIRI_VT_BENCH_GOLDEN=... DIRI_VT_BENCH_DIR=<kitten captures> <bench binary> --bench
#
# Sections are "[workload payload-sha256]": the generated payloads, and the
# kitten 0.48 `__benchmark__` captures (one repetition each) the published
# numbers use. Regenerate only from a known-good reference commit, never
# from the code being measured, and name that commit here. Any PR that
# changes history retention must regenerate this file in the same PR.

